1 tsp oil
Butter, salt and pepper, to serve', 'Scrub the sweet potatoes, prick them a few times with a fork and rub with the oil.
Set them on the foil-lined June pan; they drip sugary juice.
Oven: Bake 400°F, middle shelf, 45 to 60 minutes, until a knife slides in with no resistance
Split open and add butter, salt and pepper.', 'This is a starter version written for the wiki, not June''s original. If you made June''s version, add its settings and tips here.', 'side, easy', 'https://juneoven.com/pages/recipe-baked-sweet-potatoes-91365903', 'https://recipe-media.juneoven.com/recipes-prod/rec_91365903-3f01-4476-b7a0-2295f19a9963.650x433.jpg', 0, 1, '2026-10-11T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-10-11T00:00:00.000Z', 'june', 1, 'June');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO revisions (recipe_id, rev, data, author, comment, ip_hash, created_at) SELECT id, 1, '{"title":"Baked Sweet Potatoes","summary":"Whole sweet potatoes, baked until soft and syrupy.","category":"Vegetables & sides","mode":"Bake","temp":"400°F","shelf":"Middle","prep":"2 min","cook":"45–60 min","servings":"4","ingredients":"4 medium sweet potatoes\n1 tsp oil\nButter, salt and pepper, to serve","steps":"Scrub the sweet potatoes, prick them a few times with a fork and rub with the oil.\nSet them on the foil-lined June pan; they drip sugary juice.\nOven: Bake 400°F, middle shelf, 45 to 60 minutes, until a knife slides in with no resistance\nSplit open and add butter, salt and pepper.","notes":"This is a starter version written for the wiki, not June''s original. If you made June''s version, add its settings and tips here.","tags":"side, easy"}', 'Project July', 'Starter version written by Project July', '', '2026-10-11T00:00:00.000Z' FROM recipes WHERE slug = 'baked-sweet-potatoes';
